win10xbox: kernelbase exports LoadStringBaseExW

The genuine user32 (the native-GUI folders) implements LoadStringW by calling kernelbase!LoadStringBaseExW, which Wine had as
a stub: the loader bound a stub that raised EXCEPTION_WINE_STUB on the first string load, e.g. in the DllMain of Wine's crypt32
(LoadLibrary failed). LoadStringW and the new export share one loader with a language argument. Applies on top of 0004.

diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec b/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
@@ -978,7 +978,7 @@
 @ stdcall LoadPackagedLibrary(wstr long)
 @ stdcall LoadResource(long long)
 @ stdcall LoadStringA(long long ptr long)
-@ stub LoadStringBaseExW
+@ stdcall LoadStringBaseExW(long long ptr long long)
 @ stub LoadStringByReference
 @ stdcall LoadStringW(long long ptr long)
 @ stdcall LocalAlloc(long long)
diff --git a/dlls/kernelbase/string.c b/dlls/kernelbase/string.c
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/string.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/string.c
